---
title: What's Next
description: Further resources for customizing and extending the Vonage Video iOS App theme.
---

Congratulations, you have successfully completed the tutorial! Copy the public VERA backend server URL from this Codespace and paste it into the learning path to generate your certificate of completion — you don't need to keep this Codespace open or the server running afterwards.

## What You Accomplished

- Started the shared backend server in this Codespace and made its port public
- Cloned `vonage-video-ios-app` to your own machine, generated the environment constants, and ran the app in Xcode's Simulator
- Understood the structure of `VERA/Theme/semantics.json`, including its color tokens and typography sizing (font-size/line-height)
- Edited color and typography tokens in `semantics.json` and regenerated the `SemanticColors.xcassets` asset catalog with `generate-app-theme.py`
- Rebuilt the app in Xcode and confirmed your changes in the Simulator

## What's Next

Want to also enable or disable app features? Continue with the companion **Vonage Video iOS App Feature Config** tutorial — it picks up from the same local setup and walks through `VERA/Config/app-config.json`.

## Resources

- [Vonage Developer Portal](https://developer.vonage.com) — Documentation, guides, and API references for all Vonage products.
- [Vonage Video API Documentation](https://developer.vonage.com/en/video/overview) — In-depth guides for the Video API.
- [vonage-video-ios-app on GitHub](https://github.com/Vonage/vonage-video-ios-app) — Source code, full README with all configuration options, and contribution guidelines.
